{
  "action_id": "rewrite_priority",
  "rationale": "The reported baseline maximum arrival is 1.73 ns on request-to-onehot paths. With independently mapped fixed blocks, rewrite_mux leaves those paths unchanged and cannot reduce that maximum. rewrite_priority targets them directly, replacing encode-then-decode logic with grouped winner generation. It preserves highest-bit priority and the zero-request outputs (valid=0, index=0, onehot=1), while leaving mux behavior unchanged. This is the structurally justified choice for improving whole-design arrival, although compliance with the 2719.608320 um^2 area cap and the final timing cannot be confirmed without candidate mapping results."
}
